<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Imagina's colours for the screens of Thunderbird (IMAGINA.md, «Colores»): the Material 3 roles of the
    design system «Light Craft» (resources/ui/tokens.css in Imagina), in the light and the dark theme.

    The names are Thunderbird's (core/ui/legacy/theme2/thunderbird/.../colors.xml): a resource of the app
    replaces the one of a library with the same name, so Theme2.Thunderbird.Light and .Dark, and with them
    the XML screens, take these colours without touching a file of Thunderbird. ImaginaBoltTheme (Compose)
    reads the same resources, so there is one palette. The names with Info, Success and Warning are not in
    Thunderbird's XML: only Compose's theme uses them.

    How the roles come from the design system (light / dark):
      primary                accent #0F766E / #2DD4BF, text on it on-accent #FFFFFF / #0B2B28
      primaryContainer       accent-soft #CCFBF1 / #123C38, text on it accent-soft-text #134E4A / #99F6E4
      secondary              accent-hover #115E59 / #5EEAD4 (the selection, secondaryContainer, is accent-soft)
      surface                canvas #F8F7F4 / #111219; the surface containers go from white / #1A1B25 (the
                             surface of cards) to surface-muted and border, so the top bar is a little apart
                             from the list
      onSurface              ink #1A1B25 / #F3F2EE; onSurfaceVariant ink-secondary #474B57 / #C9CBD3
      outline, outlineVariant border-control #8A8880 / #6E7284, border-strong #D4D2CD / #3A3D4E
      error, info, success, warning   danger, info, success and warning, with their -soft background
      surfaceContainerLow    surface #FFFFFF / #1A1B25: the cards, the bottom sheets and the drawer, which Material
                             paints with this role, are white on the canvas, as the design system's cards, sidebar
                             and drawer
    The brand teal #0D9488 is not here: it is only for logos and graphics, never for text or buttons.

    The text pairs keep 4.5:1 in both themes; ImaginaColorsTest checks it, so a change here that breaks it fails.
-->
